  <page_number>41</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Auxilium dare fœderatis.</i></p>
    <p><i>Illum sequutus sum puer exulem</i></p>
    <p><i>Exul tenellus, quum vagus exteras</i></p>
    <p><i>Lustraret oras, perditisque</i></p>
    <p><i>Rebus opem peteret negatam.</i></p>
    <p><i>Non iuuit illum gratia Cæsaris</i></p>
    <p><i>Cognata, magnis seditionibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Tunc occupati, non fauores</i></p>
    <p><i>Teutonicæ potuere Gentis</i></p>
    <p><i>Seruare. Tandem tristibus imparem</i></p>
    <p><i>Curis, egentem, optata necessitas</i></p>
    <p><i>Lethi recepit, meque fidum</i></p>
    <p><i>Exilij comitem paterni</i></p>
    <p><i>Neglexit atrox. Aft pauidum erigit,</i></p>
    <p><i>Tristemque rerum sors variabilis</i></p>
    <p><i>Solata, dixit: Te labores,</i></p>
    <p><i>Te mala multa manent: secundos</i></p>
    <p><i>Sed fortis aude casibus exitus</i></p>
    <p><i>Sperare duris Cæsareos cliens</i></p>
    <p><i>Inter clientes, tam moleftis</i></p>
    <p><i>Temporibus patiens vocari.</i></p>
    <p><i>Vixi superbis nutibus obsequens</i></p>
    <p><i>Supplex potentum liminibus virum:</i></p>
    <p><i>Multaque longos per labores</i></p>
    <p><i>Sollicitum expediere curæ.</i></p>
    <p><i>Si quem feroci verbere contudit</i></p>
    <p><i>Fortuna sæuis læta negotiis,</i></p>
    <p><i>Sero quiescit, sera duris</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse lines are printed with long s rendered as s; some words, such as "Lustraret" and "Gentis", are set with small uncertainties in the scan. The running head is in small capitals with the number 41 at top right.</notes>
</page>
